00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,659
Slide 18 contrasts "SYNCHRONOUS VS.

2
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:05,620
ASYNCHRONOUS" execution.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:16,737
On the left card tagged "BLOCKING", we see "Synchronous Execution." In a synchronous model, every API request blocks the main thread.

4
00:00:16,737 --> 00:00:25,040
If a database query or web scrape takes 45 seconds, the human user is frozen staring at a loading spinner.

5
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:34,048
Now look at the right card tagged "NON-BLOCKING": "Asynchronous Pipeline." When an event occurs, it is pushed to a background event queue.

6
00:00:34,048 --> 00:00:40,550
The agent processes it independently in the cloud and notifies you only when the finished artifact is ready.

7
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:46,201
Asynchronous architecture is the vital secret of sleep-free computing.

8
00:00:46,201 --> 00:00:51,790
It frees the human from waiting loops and allows systems to scale horizontally.

9
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:57,410
Always design your agent workflows with non-blocking, event-driven queues!

